WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.590
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:13.370
Last time: sequencing = the right order

3
00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:21.510
Chapter 3 · Loops

4
00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:32.880
Same thing, again and again? There's a trick!

5
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:39.810
Sports Day! Robo, cheer for our team!

6
00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:51.300
Clap · Clap · Clap · Clap · Clap

7
00:00:51.300 --> 00:01:01.480
100 claps? That's a LOT of writing!

8
00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:08.700
Is there a shorter way? Think!

9
00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:21.310
"Clap 5 times." Same claps, much shorter!

10
00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:25.530
That trick is called a LOOP

11
00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:39.110
Loop = do the same steps again and again

12
00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:50.530
Repeat 5 times: clap

13
00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:59.490
Round and round, like a running track

14
00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:04.870
Why are loops helpful?

15
00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:18.140
10 lines → just 1 loop!

16
00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:34.450
Short · Saves time · Fewer mistakes

17
00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:42.210
Kind 1: repeat a fixed number of times

18
00:02:42.210 --> 00:03:00.200
One over: repeat 6 times: bowl one ball

19
00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:10.870
Repeat 20 times: skip

20
00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:19.360
You choose: 2, 5, 20… not always 10!

21
00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:24.890
Kind 2: repeat UNTIL something is done

22
00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:34.280
Stir until the sugar melts

23
00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:44.110
Brush each tooth until all are clean

24
00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:55.690
It stops when the job is done!

25
00:03:55.690 --> 00:04:11.570
Which one is a loop?

26
00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:28.440
Stirring until the sugar melts = a loop!

27
00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:40.770
Five jumps. Which loop is the same?

28
00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:51.480
Repeat 5 times: jump

29
00:04:51.480 --> 00:05:03.440
A square: 4 sides, 4 corners

30
00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:17.330
Draw, turn · Draw, turn · Draw, turn · Draw, turn

31
00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:28.330
Same 2 steps, 4 times. A pattern!

32
00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:32.230
Your turn: practice check

33
00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:41.340
Write a loop to draw a square

34
00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:55.740
Repeat 4 times: draw a side, turn

35
00:05:55.740 --> 00:06:00.920
Loop = do it again

36
00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:05.510
Repeat N times, or repeat until done

37
00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:08.740
Loops keep steps short and save time

38
00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:14.990
Square: repeat 4 times: draw a side, turn

39
00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:22.230
Chapter 3 done!

40
00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:29.030
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
